Falsifies `block_driver_roles::verification::a_bounded_wait_stops_at_its_bound`.

The defect: the bounded wait counts with an inclusive range, `0..=wakeups` in place of
`0..wakeups`. That is one wakeup past the bound, and for a bound of zero, one wakeup where none
was allowed.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(wakeups <= bound)`, on a run where no wakeup sees the
used index move.

diff --git a/components/src/block_driver_roles.rs b/components/src/block_driver_roles.rs
--- a/components/src/block_driver_roles.rs
+++ b/components/src/block_driver_roles.rs
@@ -684,3 +684,3 @@ fn used_ring_moved(
     match bound {
-        Some(wakeups) => (0..wakeups).any(|_| wake_and_read() != used_before),
+        Some(wakeups) => (0..=wakeups).any(|_| wake_and_read() != used_before),
         None => loop {
